            <ArticleTitle>Paediatric coronary artery bypass grafting for coronary hypoperfusion late after arterial switch operation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>460-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1017/S1047951111000138</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of left main coronary artery stenosis is presented in a boy late after an arterial switch operation, with significant ischaemia during exercise with good collateralisation through the right coronary artery. The problem was successfully managed with minimally invasive off-pump coronary artery bypass through median re-sternotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
